The intermediate shape EF materializes for a feed projection: it holds the  value object
(materialized through its converter) and the full body, so the SQL projection stays translatable;
 completes the mapping client-side.

Handles : load the current user's tracked User
aggregate, apply the domain mutation (User.UpdateNotificationPreferences with a fresh
), and save. A thin orchestrator — the value object is the invariant.

Handles : load the current user's tracked User
aggregate, apply the domain mutation (User.UpdateNotificationPreferences with a fresh
), and save. A thin orchestrator — the value object is the invariant.

Handles as the exact ADR 0013 §2.5 orchestration, keeping the store and the DB consistent with no orphan on the happy path:
persist + validate the new bytes ( — the authoritative gate);
load the current user, capture the old key, the new key, and save;
if the save committed and there was an old key, best-effort delete the replaced file.
If step 2 throws AFTER step 1 saved bytes, the just-saved key is best-effort deleted in the catch to avoid an orphan, then the exception is rethrown (the DB is left unchanged). A best-effort delete failure logs a Warning and never fails the request (orphan-sweep deferred, §13).

