Handles with the three-tier, LLM-free serve order (ADR 0018 §4):
(a) served cache hit → return it (), the steady-state fast path;
(b) cache miss → the latest AIRecommendationHistory row (indexed Top(1) over (UserId, GeneratedAtUtc)), parsed from its self-contained OutputSummary envelope (). This is a READ ONLY — a query never re-warms the cache (a write); the next precompute re-warms it. A corrupt/old-schema envelope falls through, it never throws;
(c) no usable history → the deterministic () so the page always renders.
The handler has NO dependency by design (the zero-page-load-LLM contract). The cache read is additionally wrapped defensively: the adapter already degrades internally, but "never 500 on serve" is a hard exit criterion, so even a throwing cache falls through to history/heuristic.

