The Application implementation of over (cached) and the shared (Phase 5 design §9). It reuses the same taste projection + seen-exclusion set as the AI pipeline, then fans out with honest, per-tier template reasons:
"more like your highest-rated" — GetRecommendationsAsync per seed, reason "Because you rated {Title} {Rating}/10." (the seed's own title/rating, which is why the seed keys and the profile's top-rated titles are consumed in parallel);
"popular in your favorite genres" — DiscoverByGenreAsync, reason "Popular in {Genre}.";
global-popular top-up (and the WHOLE story for a brand-new, no-signal user) — GetPopularAsync then GetTopRatedAsync, reason "Popular on Cinora right now.".
Every accumulated title is excluded if seen, deduplicated by (TmdbId, Media), and the pool is capped to . Card metadata comes from the TMDB summary; there is no model and no dependency — the zero-LLM guarantee holds by construction.

